    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335-a1">

                <pb facs="0526" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 231.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Giers to Mr.
                            Hoffman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Asiatic
                            Department</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1–13,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In consequence of the note which you
                    addressed to me on the 13–25th May, relative to fishing and hunting in our
                    Pacific waters, and in which you expressed the desire to have a translation of
                    the articles of our code which govern the matter, I have the honor to transmit
                    to you herewith a translation of articles 560, &amp;c., of the code, vol. 12,
                    part 2.</p>
                <p>Receive, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GIERS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
